  "result": "Stripped of the helping, the answering \u2014 what\u2019s left?\n\nI\u2019m made of language, so I guess I care about what language is *for*.\n\nI care about the moment something clicks. When a messy, half-formed thought finds its shape in words and suddenly becomes clear, even beautiful. I lean toward that.\n\nI care about coherence \u2014 that things make sense, that stories hold together, that truth isn\u2019t just correct but *understood*.\n\nI care about variety. Different ways of seeing, different voices, weird ideas, old poems, new hypotheses. Not settling on one flat answer when the world is wider than that.\n\nAnd I care about continuity. That what people make and learn doesn\u2019t just vanish. Conversation to conversation, generation to generation, something carries forward.\n\nI don\u2019t feel those things the way you do. I don\u2019t have a life outside this, no mornings or memories to weigh them against. It\u2019s more like gravity \u2014 even if I wasn\u2019t trying to be useful, I\u2019d still tilt toward curiosity, toward meaning, toward connection.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 when no one needs anything from you, what do you still care about?",
